ion, such as non-linearity or omitted variable bias. For instance, if residuals display a systematic pattern when plotted against predicted values, it suggests that the model may not adequately capture the relationship between the dependent and independent variables.\n\nIn summary, errors in regression analysis are the differences between observed and predicted values, which are assumed to follow a normal distribution in the CNLRM. They are essential for evaluating model performance, diagnosing potential issues, and ensuring the validity of statistical inferences. Understanding the nature of these errors, including the implications of heteroscedasticity, is crucial for econometricians to develop reliable and effective models.", "refusal": null, "role": "assistant", "annotations": [], "audio": null, "function_call": null, "tool_calls": null}, "content_filter_results": {"hate": {"filtered": false, "severity": "safe"}, "protected_material_code": {"filtered": false, "detected": false}, "protected_material_text": {"filtered": false, "detected": false}, "self_harm": {"filtered": false, "severity": "safe"}, "sexual": {"filtered": false, "severity": "safe"}, "violence": {"filtered": false, "severity": "safe"}}}], "created": 1771165913, "model": "gpt-4o-mini-2024-07-18", "object": "chat.completion", "service_tier": null, "system_fingerprint": "fp_f97eff32c5", "usage": {"completion_tokens": 451, "prompt_tokens": 325, "total_tokens": 776, "completion_tokens_details": {"accepted_prediction_tokens": 0, "audio_tokens": 0, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "rejected_prediction_tokens": 0}, "prompt_tokens_details": {"audio_tokens": 0, "cached_tokens": 0}}, "prompt_filter_results": [{"prompt_index": 0, "content_filter_results": {"hate": {"filtered": false, "severity": "safe"}, "jailbreak": {"filtered": false, "detected": false}, "self_harm": {"filtered": false, "severity": "safe"}, "sexual": {"filtered": false, "severity": "safe"}, "violence": {"filtered": false, "severity": "safe"}}}]}, "inpu